.IX Title "LR_RUN.IN 1"
.TH LR_RUN.IN 1 2025-09-28 "Lire 2.1.1" "LogReport's Lire Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "نام (NAME)"
lr_run \- run a Lire program and deal with the logging output
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBlr_run\fR \fIprogram\fR \fIarguments\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBlr_run\fR runs \fIprogram\fR, and redirects \fIprogram\fR\*(Aqs stderr output
to \fBlogger\fR\|(1). It parses \fIprograms\fR logging output, and sets \fBlogger\fR\|(1)\*(Aqs 
flags accordingly.
.PP
\&\fBlr_run\fR gets configuration from \fIsysconfdir\fR/lire/defaults. In case
\&\*(Aqlr_logging_method\*(Aq is set to \*(Aqstderr\*(Aq, \fBlogger\fR\|(1) is not involved:
logging output gets redirected to stderr. In case \*(Aqlr_debug\*(Aq is set to
the empty string, messages with loglevel debug and info get
suppressed. The configuration variable \*(Aqlr_logging_facility\*(Aq is used to find
\&\fBlogger\fR\|(1)\*(Aqs facility.
.SH "نکات (NOTES)"
.IX Header "NOTES"
\&\fIprogram\fR\*(Aqs output on stderr should be in format
\&\fIsuperservice\fR \fIservice\fR \fIid\fR \fIprogramname\fR \fIlevel\fR \fImessage\fR. \fIlevel\fR
should be one of: 
emerg (system is unusable), alert (action must be taken immediately), crit 
(critical conditions), err (error conditions), warning (warning conditions),
notice (normal, but significant, condition), info (informational message),
debug (debug\-level message). See \fBsyslog\fR\|(3).
.PP
\&\fIid\fR can be used to tag each Lire job, so that these can get tracked. 
\&\fIprogramname\fR should be the name of the program which generated the log line.
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
To process a Postfix log and display the report as text, use
.PP
.Vb 1
\& $ lr_run lr_log2report postfix < /var/log/mail.log
.Ve
.PP
To process a Postfix log and create the report in HTML (packed up in a tar
archive), use:
.PP
.Vb 1
\& $ lr_run lr_log2report \-o html postfix < /var/log/mail.log > postfix.tar
.Ve
